  <running_head>CASTIGATIO PARAL.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">confolabantur lugentes cibo &amp; potu,</l>
    <l n="2">unde <i>poculum confolationum dictum</i> a</l>
    <l n="3">Jeremia cap. 16: 7. &amp; <i>cibus ad confo-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>landum</i>, ibidem. Hoc erat magnum</l>
    <l n="5">humanitatis officium, &amp; non nisi ad</l>
    <l n="6">levandum luctum institutum. In</l>
    <l n="7">capite ergo hoc quarto inter cæte-</l>
    <l n="8">ras admonitiones (nam totum</l>
    <l n="9">hoc caput est <i>παιδευτικόν</i> &amp; mora-</l>
    <l n="10">le) filio præcipit, ut hoc humanitatis</l>
    <l n="11">&amp; beneficentiæ officium non negligat,</l>
    <l n="12">sed lugentibus copiosè e suo admini-</l>
    <l n="13">stret. Constat autem hoc præceptum</l>
    <l n="14">meris ornamentis rhetoricis. <i>Effunde</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">(methaphora) id est, copiosè largire,</l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>panes tuos</i> (synechdoche speciei) id</l>
    <l n="17">est, cibum &amp; potum: <i>super sepulturam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>justorum</i> (metonymia subiecti) id est,</l>
    <l n="19">iustis sepelientibus parentes aut pro-</l>
    <l n="20">pinquos suos. Nullum hic vestigium</l>
    <l n="21">purgatorii, nullum oblationum pro</l>
    <l n="22">defunctis.</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">Deinde argumentatur ex 2. Mach.</l>
    <l n="24">cap.</l>
  </main_text>
